{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#842","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#842","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#842\",\"parent_revision\":\"1bd52e9cd2a634dc033cc3ce650c5482a2d64f66d5e4d330955ee0b8594b6a22\",\"root_revision\":\"1bd52e9cd2a634dc033cc3ce650c5482a2d64f66d5e4d330955ee0b8594b6a22\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: 2026-05-16\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nbacklog_list filters by title, type, topic, section, and status \u2014 but has no way to search item bodies or descriptions. Items that describe a concept (e.g. \\\"migrate python3-development steps into development-harness\\\") but don't contain the search terms in their title are invisible to the MCP. This caused a failed investigation where the correct item existed but couldn't be found via any available filter.\\n\\nAdd a `body` (or `search`) parameter to backlog_list that performs full-text substring search across the item description and body sections (Groomed, Research, etc.). Should work in both the MCP tool and the CLI (`backlog.py list --search \\\"...\\\"`).\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAssessment date: 2026-04-23\\n\\n| # | Condition | Status | Source |\\n|---|-----------|--------|--------|\\n| 1 | `search` parameter already in MCP tool schema | AVAILABLE | backlog_list tool description observed in this session |\\n| 2 | CLI `backlog.py list --search` implementation | DERIVABLE | Check `.claude/skills/backlog/scripts/backlog.py` |\\n| 3 | Whether body search was already implemented | DERIVABLE | Run `backlog_list(search='some body term')` to verify |\\n\\nVerdict: LIKELY ALREADY IMPLEMENTED \u2014 `search` parameter visible in backlog_list MCP schema with full OR/AND/NOT support. Verify and close if confirmed.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **backlog_list: add full-text body/description search to mcp and cli** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation \u2014 backlog_list title-only filter missed items during investigation\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-18\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-23)\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\nP2 Feature. Likely already done. Verify and close.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- `backlog_list` accepts a `search` (or `body`) parameter that performs full-text substring search across item description and body sections\\n- Search works in both the MCP tool and the CLI (`backlog.py list --search '...'`)\\n- Items matching on body content appear in results even if their title doesn't contain the search term\\n- Verification note: as of 2026-04-23, the `backlog_list` MCP tool description already shows a `search` parameter with full-text search support (including OR/AND/NOT operators). If this is already implemented, this item should be closed as done.\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` \u2014 verify search param exists\\n- `.claude/skills/backlog/scripts/backlog.py` \u2014 verify --search CLI flag\\n\\n### Story\\n\\nAs a backlog_list caller, I need to search item bodies and descriptions for text patterns so I can find items that describe a concept but don't use the search term in their title.\\n\",\"digest\":\"8f50fe551411680b50b13da544a6ab70a6aa79378aedcbc1f4ddc4d3949aee6b\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVCP86g\"}"}